1
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:08,825
NARRATOR: Previously: Embarrassment broke into his friend's house to catch a thing that should never have left its cage.

2
00:00:09,175 --> 00:00:12,303
EMBARRASSMENT: Okay. Okay. Nobody saw anything. Walk home. Nice and normal.

3
00:00:13,303 --> 00:00:17,004
EMBARRASSMENT (thinking): Oh God. Act natural. Act like I'm in control of the situation.

4
00:00:17,504 --> 00:00:20,304
[The street is wrecked. Trash cans, lights, debris. He did all of this.]

5
00:00:22,104 --> 00:00:26,779
EMBARRASSMENT: Hey, boss! How you doing? Yeah, it's all good. Got the thing right here. Nothing to be afraid of. Hehe.

6
00:00:27,879 --> 00:00:29,882
ASSISTANT: Shall I process his termination, Doctor?

7
00:00:30,482 --> 00:00:31,322
DR. CONTEMPT: Not yet.

8
00:00:31,922 --> 00:00:35,710
DR. CONTEMPT: He's friends with the one who got bitten. That makes him useful.

9
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:36,734
ASSISTANT: Do we tell him?

10
00:00:36,934 --> 00:00:37,531
DR. CONTEMPT: No.

11
00:00:38,931 --> 00:00:42,910
EMBARRASSMENT: Doctor Contempt, I just want to say how sorry I am. I feel terrible about-

12
00:00:42,910 --> 00:00:45,191
DR. CONTEMPT: Your feelings are not relevant here.

13
00:00:45,391 --> 00:00:51,315
DR. CONTEMPT: You lost a level five specimen. You destroyed a street. You broke into a civilian's home.

14
00:00:51,515 --> 00:00:53,768
EMBARRASSMENT: Technically he's my friend, so it was more of a visit-

15
00:00:53,768 --> 00:00:59,829
DR. CONTEMPT: Your friend was in contact with the specimen. That is the only reason you still have a badge.

16
00:01:00,329 --> 00:01:01,378
DR. CONTEMPT: You'll carry this.

17
00:01:01,578 --> 00:01:02,225
EMBARRASSMENT: A tracker?

18
00:01:02,425 --> 00:01:04,967
DR. CONTEMPT: A recorder. Everything he says, we hear.

19
00:01:05,167 --> 00:01:06,339
EMBARRASSMENT: Isn't that a little... shady?

20
00:01:06,539 --> 00:01:09,814
DR. CONTEMPT: You can carry it. Or you can clear out your desk tonight.

21
00:01:10,014 --> 00:01:12,098
EMBARRASSMENT: No! No. Recording. I love recording. Big fan.

22
00:01:12,298 --> 00:01:13,787
DR. CONTEMPT: Good. And don't tell him.

23
00:01:14,687 --> 00:01:15,895
EMBARRASSMENT: HEY, BUDDY! I BROUGHT SNACKS!

24
00:01:16,095 --> 00:01:17,887
TIREDNESS: Why are you talking to your pocket?

25
00:01:18,087 --> 00:01:19,061
EMBARRASSMENT: I'm not! Ha. Haha.

26
00:01:19,261 --> 00:01:22,596
EMBARRASSMENT (thinking): Be cool. Be nice. Don't let him say anything weird. They're listening.

27
00:01:22,896 --> 00:01:24,309
TIREDNESS: So that thing that bit me-

28
00:01:24,309 --> 00:01:25,498
EMBARRASSMENT: WHAT A NICE DAY IT IS!

29
00:01:25,998 --> 00:01:26,808
TIREDNESS: It's raining.

30
00:01:27,008 --> 00:01:30,860
EMBARRASSMENT (thinking): Don't let him implicate himself. Don't give them anything they can use.

31
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:35,014
EMBARRASSMENT: So how's the arm? You feel totally normal, right? Normal is good. Say normal.

32
00:01:35,214 --> 00:01:38,519
TIREDNESS: I feel weird. I could hear your heartbeat from downstairs.

33
00:01:39,119 --> 00:01:41,321
EMBARRASSMENT: HA! He's joking! Funny guy! Very normal guy!

34
00:01:42,121 --> 00:01:44,676
EMBARRASSMENT: Well! I should go. Lots of very normal stuff to do-

35
00:01:46,276 --> 00:01:48,076
[Beep. Beep. A little red light.]

36
00:01:48,376 --> 00:01:51,959
EMBARRASSMENT: That's my... pager. It's an old pager. Pagers are back. Very retro.

37
00:01:52,159 --> 00:01:52,726
TIREDNESS: Cool.

38
00:01:53,726 --> 00:01:54,749
EMBARRASSMENT: Okay bye love you see you later!

39
00:01:55,426 --> 00:01:58,881
TIREDNESS (thinking): That was a recorder. Somebody wants to hear what I say.

40
00:01:59,181 --> 00:02:01,780
TIREDNESS (thinking): He's scared of somebody. And it isn't me.

41
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:04,344
TIREDNESS (thinking): And it has something to do with that thing.

42
00:02:07,644 --> 00:02:09,854
TIREDNESS: Calm Corp. 'Feel less.' Great slogan.

43
00:02:10,954 --> 00:02:12,862
TIREDNESS: They bugged my friend to spy on me.

44
00:02:13,062 --> 00:02:14,726
TIREDNESS: Fine. I'll go see them myself.

45
00:02:15,226 --> 00:02:18,208
TIREDNESS: I'm not sneaking in. I'm walking in the front door.

46
00:02:18,408 --> 00:02:20,796
TIREDNESS: Nobody stops a guy who looks this tired.
